Same fixes as rules_rust_bindgen-0.71.3.patch, against the version WORKSPACE
mode is stuck on (rules_rust dropped WORKSPACE support after 0.63.0).  Keep the
two patches in sync.

rust_bindgen filters the cc_toolchain's flags down to an allowlist that omits
-idirafter, which is how toolchains_llvm passes the sysroot and builtin include
directories; without them bindgen parses against a truncated include path.  What
does survive is a C++ compile's flags feeding a C parse, so silence the
resulting "argument unused during compilation" noise.

--- a/private/bindgen.bzl
+++ b/private/bindgen.bzl
@@ -254,6 +254,11 @@
     # Configure Clang Arguments
     args.add("--")
 
+    # The CC toolchain's flags are written for its own language mode.  bindgen
+    # parses headers as C, where flags like -nostdinc++ do nothing, so clang
+    # warns about each one and buries the real output.
+    args.add("-Wno-unused-command-line-argument")
+
     compile_variables = cc_common.create_compile_variables(
         cc_toolchain = cc_toolchain,
         feature_configuration = feature_configuration,
@@ -280,6 +285,7 @@
     param_flags_known_to_clang = (
         "-I",
         "-iquote",
+        "-idirafter",
         "-isystem",
         "--sysroot",
         "--gcc-toolchain",
